# Mongoose

`autoIndex: false`. Startup calls `createIndexes()` and does not call `syncIndexes()`. Model functions return `.lean()` plain objects, or `null`. They do not throw `DOCTOR_NOT_FOUND` or `PATIENT_NOT_FOUND`.

Patient reads include `deletedAt: null`. The public patient resource has no `deletedAt`. Indexes on patients are partial on `{ deletedAt: null }`.

| Collection | Indexes |
| --- | --- |
| admins | unique `{ email: 1 }` |
| sessions | unique `{ tokenHash: 1 }`, TTL `{ expiresAt: 1 }` with `expireAfterSeconds: 0`, `{ adminId: 1 }` |
| doctors | unique `{ email: 1 }`; `{ createdAt: -1, _id: -1 }`; `{ specialization: 1, createdAt: -1 }` and `{ hospital: 1, createdAt: -1 }`, both with collation `{ locale: "en", strength: 2 }` |
| patients | `{ doctorId: 1, registeredAt: -1, _id: -1 }`, `{ registeredAt: -1, _id: -1 }`, `{ condition: 1, registeredAt: -1 }`, each partial `{ deletedAt: null }` |

Pass the collation only on queries that filter specialization or hospital. Escape search text in the service with `escapeRegex` before it becomes a regex. Store emails lowercase. List queries use `find` + `countDocuments` together, with `skip` / `limit`. Page size stays at most 50.

Explain-plan checks for the three indexed patient shapes must show `IXSCAN`.
